ort from our team and a  community of like-minded students that  you can interact with and potentially  design even group projects together with  them  so on the portal you will be able to  utilize our system to guide you through  all of the steps that are typically  included in preparing a poster  presentation and here i have a brief  recording of how this is possible to do  on the portal itself so the first step  would be to complete your profile  then you would have to add your bio and  connect to your orc id or your social  media  and after you do that you will have to  earn 10 000 points by practicing  different types of analyses that we  describe in programs and courses  and complete a course  that speaks about the way that you can  utilize bioinformatics to do a research  project  now after that you can start your own  project  and the project will have several  different sections including an overview  kind of reproducible projects include a  reference data set that is curated and  prepared  so we will go through the process of  submitting that data set on dataverse  and explaining the metadata  we will then talk about all the standard  sections like abstract introduction  methods results discussion and  conclusion including a list of  references and acknowledgments at the  end  now as a result of completing such a  project you will be able to add that  project to your resume or present it at  a poster conference  and so here we have several examples of  people that have submitted either as a  preprint  others have published in the  undergraduate  journals  and others have even used some of the  results that they were working on in  their ongoing research studies  some just use that example to  train  and acquire skills as well  but what's important is that at the end  of the summer  in august we will have our virtual omix  research symposium  this symposium is a bi-annual event that  we organize together with our partners  where we invite experts from  bioinformatics research  in industry and academia as well as  experts in bioinformatics education to  discuss pressing topics and advances in  bioinformatics but also we provide a  platform for students faculty and  researchers to present those posters and  get feedback specific feedback on their  projects and how to take those projects  further so it's really an opportunity to  find mentors and communities that you  can join and learn about how to  implement these this kind of training  wherever you are  so again with that i am happy to take  any questions that you might have  i will briefly mention  the process of  again registration  so for any one of you that is coming  from nepi from the national association  of idea principal investigators  one of your questions might be  well how do i know that i am from nepy  right how do i know that i am affiliated  with the nappy institution the way to  know that is to go to  nepi.org  which is the website that lists out  all of the institutions  and all of the states that participate  in this program  so if just scroll down a little bit you  will see this map  on the map if you click on any one of  these you will find  a description  and if you scroll down beyond that you  will also see all of the active  principal investigators  so to participate in the program from  nepi  uh you have to be a member of the  institution where the pi is at  right so if your  lab pi  is a member of nepe that's great  if in your institution there is api that  is enough right so really this is just  the institution so for example in  louisiana people from lsu  lsu hsc  et cetera now we only have a limited  number of nepy licenses that are going  to be covered a hundred percent  and that's 50  and then we have an additional 100 that  are going to be offered at 75 off so  that's still a significant discount and  so i i um i think it would be useful if  you also don't know uh whether your  institution is a part of nepi you can  simply search  for th